<http://data.silknow.org/object/eebc37de-3d69-3212-b639-46478b1269e0>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Center top, Saint Catharine, center bottom, Virgin and child, variety of birds, animals, flowers and plants and geometric ornaments scattered over ground. Worked with white cotton, polychrome silks and gold and silver metal thread in tent, rococo and  knot stitches. Eyes of two birds and of Saint Catharine formed by jet beads. Hair of Saint Catharine and of lion made of looped threads. In lower left center: 1669 MAÖ. Worn in many places. Several small holes."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/2f99e105-32c9-302e-814c-ecb602d7aef8> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ba1a72e9-8034-3972-868c-c2f6f8a0152c> ;
